1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,580
A sound soul dwells within a sound mind and a sound body.

2
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:18,020
Soul and I traveled to Italy to collect Kishan souls for an extracurricular lesson.

3
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:24,460
We were able to meet our quota for the lesson.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
But just as we were about to leave, I sensed a troubling soul wavelength nearby.

5
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Something told me that I shouldn't open that door, but I didn't listen.

6
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Inside, we found a soul who had crossed beyond the realm of humanity.

7
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Meister and weapon is one, on the verge of becoming a Kishu.

8
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,000
We tried to fight them, but...

9
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,000
We tried to fight them, but...

10
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,000
I screwed up.

11
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,000
I screwed up.

12
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,000
I screwed up.

13
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Kishu

14
00:01:38,000 --> 00:02:07,980
I'll see you next time.

15
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:37,980
Thank you.

16
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,560
繋いだ魂の火が胸を刺すなら

17
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:49,360
言葉よりもっと強い響きが今聞こえるか

18
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:54,480
やっと理由は途絶びに突きつけられて

19
00:02:54,480 --> 00:03:00,200
触れた瞬間の傷の分だけ確かになれる

20
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:35,620
ソウル!

21
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:40,440
ソウル!

22
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:43,720
ゴーオン クロナ

23
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:45,060
フィニッシュ

24
00:03:45,060 --> 00:03:52,360
メドゥサ ウィッチ

25
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:53,620
ウィッチ ウィッチ ウィッチ ウィッチ

26
00:03:53,620 --> 00:03:57,620
ウィッチ ウィッチ ウィッチ ウィッチ

27
00:03:57,620 --> 00:04:01,180
Kill them and eat their souls,カロナ

28
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:04,480
I think I can deal with that

29
00:04:04,480 --> 00:04:05,360
ROAD Skype

30
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:08,800
Wake up.

31
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:10,600
Soul, please.

32
00:04:11,480 --> 00:04:12,560
You dumbass.

33
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:13,880
Hurry.

34
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:15,360
Get out of here.

35
00:04:16,140 --> 00:04:16,580
Okay.

36
00:04:20,660 --> 00:04:21,540
Soul.

37
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:23,440
Soul.

38
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:25,200
This is all my fault.

39
00:04:28,780 --> 00:04:30,000
What's happening?

40
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:31,580
How did that get there?

41
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:42,760
Professor Stein!

42
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:48,360
If he's here, then that blade must be...

43
00:04:57,200 --> 00:04:59,240
Your papa has arrived.

44
00:05:00,620 --> 00:05:01,740
That's right, Maka.

45
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:05,120
Take a good look at how brave and selfless your father is.

46
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:07,660
Professor Stein, is Soul all right?

47
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:09,420
The wound's very serious.

48
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:12,360
If we don't get him treatment soon, he might not make it.

49
00:05:12,760 --> 00:05:14,280
He's not even looking at me.

50
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:19,560
I gotta say, though, it was an easier fight than I expected.

51
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:26,760
I harden the blood around your wound to stop the bleeding.

52
00:05:27,260 --> 00:05:28,660
Do I get a thank you?

53
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:30,480
Yeah, thank you.

54
00:05:30,740 --> 00:05:31,900
Thank you very much!

55
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:34,080
Are you gonna make me hurt you?

56
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:35,440
Thank you very much!

57
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:39,220
Professor Stein?

58
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:39,960
Hmm?

59
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:41,400
Who are those two?

60
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:42,700
Or what are they?

61
00:05:42,700 --> 00:05:45,000
I've never seen anything like this.

62
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:48,100
That is the reason the Academy was created.

63
00:05:49,540 --> 00:05:51,700
The reason the Academy was created?

64
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:54,560
So does that mean he's a Kishin?

65
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:57,060
Technically, not yet.

66
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:59,160
But he's only one step away from it.

67
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:02,300
Listen to me, Stein.

68
00:06:02,520 --> 00:06:04,520
Take Death Scythe and find the Demon Sword.

69
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:06,560
Stop it from awakening into a Kishin.

70
00:06:07,460 --> 00:06:10,760
That is the reason you called me back to the Academy in the first place.

71
00:06:11,660 --> 00:06:13,000
I'll take care of the sword.

72
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:17,500
We cannot allow the Kishin to be reborn into the world.

73
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:20,200
Do your job well, Stein.

74
00:06:20,460 --> 00:06:21,660
I'm counting on you.

75
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:25,940
All right, then.

76
00:06:26,960 --> 00:06:28,600
Let's take care of this, shall we?

77
00:06:28,920 --> 00:06:29,420
Yeah.

78
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:39,680
Corona, quit standing there staring into space like an idiot.

79
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:43,320
If you don't get it in gear, we're going back to the sleep deprivation again.

80
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:43,680
No!

81
00:06:43,800 --> 00:06:45,900
Don't start waking me up every hour again!

82
00:06:45,900 --> 00:06:48,780
I don't like it! The dark circles under my eyes will come back,

83
00:06:48,860 --> 00:06:50,640
and I don't know how to deal with the dark circles!

84
00:06:51,760 --> 00:06:55,800
The Grim Reaper has sent his greatest meister armed with Death Scythe.

85
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:59,320
This should be a good test to see how long Krona can last.

86
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:03,440
Krona, get them now!

87
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:08,560
Spirit, can you stand against the Demon Sword?

88
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:09,660
Of course I can.

89
00:07:09,840 --> 00:07:12,020
What do you think I am, some kind of rusty old dagger?

90
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:15,100
Been a long time, hasn't it?

91
00:07:15,100 --> 00:07:16,720
Since we teamed up like this?

92
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:19,900
We're not as young as we used to be, that's for sure.

93
00:07:20,020 --> 00:07:21,920
Speak for yourself. I haven't aged a bit.

94
00:07:22,180 --> 00:07:24,120
Would you hurry up and attack already, you idiot?

95
00:07:27,580 --> 00:07:30,880
But I've never seen a man with a screw sticking out of his head before!

96
00:07:31,140 --> 00:07:33,620
I don't know how I'm supposed to deal with a guy like that!

97
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:35,500
You eat him! Swallow his soul!

98
00:07:35,500 --> 00:07:49,040
Soul Force!

99
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:49,840
Soul Force!

100
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:54,000
Professor hit him with his soul wavelength!

101
00:07:54,380 --> 00:07:55,000
Directly!

102
00:07:55,260 --> 00:07:58,060
This way he might actually be able to do some internal damage!

103
00:07:58,120 --> 00:07:58,580
Ah!

104
00:07:58,580 --> 00:08:00,660
Have another.

105
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:02,520
What?

106
00:08:03,500 --> 00:08:05,460
That's the blood from the wound we gave him.

107
00:08:12,340 --> 00:08:13,340
Mati Nido!

108
00:08:13,340 --> 00:08:18,040
Professor!

109
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:21,000
He's using every drop of his blood as a weapon.

110
00:08:21,380 --> 00:08:22,780
But how is that even possible?

111
00:08:23,260 --> 00:08:25,820
When souls are overhunted, a Demon Sword is created.

112
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:29,880
We have to stop him here and now, or he will definitely become a Kishin.

113
00:08:30,540 --> 00:08:33,540
What's more, the balance of power between these two is uneven.

114
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:36,980
The weapon's soul is clearly dominant.

115
00:08:36,980 --> 00:08:40,640
It rules over the Meister's more introverted soul, confining it.

116
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:45,060
For the moment, the Meister still has some strength left to fight back against the weapon.

117
00:08:45,540 --> 00:08:48,720
But if he should be completely swallowed up, things will get dangerous.

118
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:51,460
There's something else.

119
00:08:51,980 --> 00:08:53,680
I see a snake coiled around him.

120
00:08:53,740 --> 00:08:54,640
What's it doing there?

121
00:08:55,280 --> 00:08:59,460
If you let him hit you with that technique again, I'm gonna stick thumbtacks in your shoes.

122
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:00,140
Got it?

123
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:00,660
No!

124
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:04,520
Thumbtacks in my shoes would stick into my feet whenever I tried to walk.

125
00:09:04,640 --> 00:09:05,160
It would hurt.

126
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:06,700
I don't think I could deal with that, really.

127
00:09:06,700 --> 00:09:07,340
Look!

128
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:22,140
Oh, I see.

129
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:24,880
Professor Stein has a specific fighting style.

130
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:28,340
First he guards, using my dad only as a shield.

131
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:30,400
Then he uses his own attack.

132
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:31,680
Soul force.

133
00:09:36,700 --> 00:09:38,400
Oh, wow.

134
00:09:42,940 --> 00:09:43,540
Damn.

135
00:09:43,780 --> 00:09:44,920
A time-lag attack.

136
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:47,580
It's time to die, screwhead!

137
00:09:47,580 --> 00:09:52,020
Professor!

138
00:09:52,020 --> 00:09:52,220
Professor!

139
00:10:01,720 --> 00:10:03,880
I think I'd like to dissect you now.

140
00:10:04,880 --> 00:10:05,620
Pee-yah!

141
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:07,920
Screw yourself!

142
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:09,500
You won't live that long!

143
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:10,820
You ready?

144
00:10:10,820 --> 00:10:11,460
Yep.

145
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:19,620
We actually need them!

146
00:10:21,740 --> 00:10:22,620
Spirit run.

147
00:10:22,780 --> 00:10:23,480
Oh, dear!

148
00:10:23,740 --> 00:10:25,480
I think this is too much for me!

149
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:28,820
Let's see you stop all of these!

150
00:10:29,400 --> 00:10:31,040
Where did the screwhead freak go?

151
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:32,780
I don't see him!

152
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:33,940
Where the hell is he?

153
00:10:34,160 --> 00:10:34,680
Dammit!

154
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:41,300
He scrambled what little brains you have left!

155
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:42,380
Hurry up and snap out of it!

156
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:44,360
We can't afford another hit from his soul wavelength!

157
00:10:45,020 --> 00:10:47,820
There are stars and planets floating around me.

158
00:10:48,060 --> 00:10:50,400
I don't think I can handle astronomy right now.

159
00:10:50,740 --> 00:10:53,220
Astronomy's a lot easier to deal with than death, you moron!

160
00:10:53,220 --> 00:10:55,380
So, suck it up and come to your senses already!

161
00:10:57,100 --> 00:10:58,540
Double palm soul force!

162
00:10:59,420 --> 00:11:00,120
Twist me!

163
00:11:08,300 --> 00:11:09,340
Needles again?

164
00:11:14,460 --> 00:11:15,060
No.

165
00:11:15,660 --> 00:11:16,720
It's over now.

166
00:11:17,860 --> 00:11:20,000
I hate to say it, but you're finished.

167
00:11:20,740 --> 00:11:22,560
So much for round one.

168
00:11:23,220 --> 00:11:25,700
It looks like I'll have some more experimenting to do.

169
00:11:37,020 --> 00:11:38,280
What's happening to him?

170
00:11:39,020 --> 00:11:40,860
He's going through soul rejection.

171
00:11:42,120 --> 00:11:45,440
Your soul wavelength's reunited, but they're falling apart now.

172
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:48,780
I guess I found his limit.

173
00:11:49,740 --> 00:11:50,260
Oh, well.

174
00:11:50,420 --> 00:11:51,160
Soul protect.

175
00:11:51,820 --> 00:11:52,340
Release.

176
00:11:53,220 --> 00:12:09,220
It's another soul.

177
00:12:09,840 --> 00:12:12,100
I don't know where it came from, but I can sense it.

178
00:12:12,540 --> 00:12:13,540
I feel it, too.

179
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:15,060
It's a witch.

180
00:12:15,060 --> 00:12:15,680
I've got a bitch.

181
00:12:15,680 --> 00:12:15,980
We'll see you're in need.

182
00:12:15,980 --> 00:12:16,780
I've got shit.

183
00:12:35,980 --> 00:12:37,860
I can't see you in the village.

184
00:12:40,640 --> 00:12:41,020
It's another wish.

185
00:12:41,020 --> 00:12:42,420
Oh, I'm sad.

186
00:12:42,420 --> 00:12:59,580
A witch, huh?

187
00:13:00,340 --> 00:13:02,200
Yes, and one with a strong soul.

188
00:13:02,640 --> 00:13:03,560
Very powerful.

189
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:08,680
My guess is she's the one who put that weapon inside the kid's body, too.

190
00:13:09,740 --> 00:13:11,420
That's the witch's soul up there?

191
00:13:12,420 --> 00:13:13,700
But how?

192
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:16,500
I should have felt a soul like that before now.

193
00:13:16,940 --> 00:13:18,420
It's incredibly strong.

194
00:13:19,160 --> 00:13:20,040
Soul protect.

195
00:13:20,820 --> 00:13:22,040
What is that?

196
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:24,160
It's advanced magic.

197
00:13:24,580 --> 00:13:25,960
Not all witches can use it.

198
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:29,940
The technique encloses the area around the soul with magic.

199
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,580
This blocks the soul's wavelength.

200
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:36,440
The witch is camouflaged, and her soul appears to be that of a normal human.

201
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:39,180
So that's the soul of a real witch?

202
00:13:39,180 --> 00:13:43,880
Mama defeated something like that in order to turn Papa into a death site?

203
00:13:46,060 --> 00:13:46,700
Pathetic.

204
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:48,580
Krona is such a weakling.

205
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:50,680
I'll have to punish him later.

206
00:13:52,180 --> 00:13:55,020
Snake, snake, cobra, cobra.

207
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:59,400
Snake, snake, cobra, cobra.

208
00:13:59,400 --> 00:14:02,760
But before I go, I'll punish you, too.

209
00:14:04,080 --> 00:14:05,140
Won't that be fun?

210
00:14:07,140 --> 00:14:08,120
Vector Arrows!

211
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:19,640
Let's go, soul residents!

212
00:14:19,640 --> 00:14:19,880
Yes!

213
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:24,520
Witch hunter!

214
00:14:24,520 --> 00:14:35,300
Quite impressive.

215
00:14:35,300 --> 00:14:55,680
I just dropped by on a little errand.

216
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:59,240
Who would have thought I'd run into the DWMA's legendary Meister?

217
00:14:59,580 --> 00:15:00,840
And Death Scythe, too.

218
00:15:00,980 --> 00:15:02,460
What an unexpected pleasure.

219
00:15:02,460 --> 00:15:05,820
I would love to stay and play with you kids a little longer.

220
00:15:06,300 --> 00:15:07,900
But I'm afraid I can't.

221
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:09,820
Perhaps we can all play another time.

222
00:15:11,020 --> 00:15:11,980
Hold it, lady!

223
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:14,040
No, it's okay.

224
00:15:15,720 --> 00:15:17,040
Let's leave her for now.

225
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:19,440
I'm more worried about soul.

226
00:15:25,460 --> 00:15:25,980
Soul.

227
00:15:25,980 --> 00:15:26,060
Soul.

228
00:15:26,060 --> 00:15:26,100
Soul.

229
00:15:32,460 --> 00:15:32,900
Soul.

230
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:37,500
Soul.

231
00:15:37,500 --> 00:15:48,480
Come on. Let's go home, Maka.

232
00:15:59,040 --> 00:16:02,320
Interesting. Those two had a pretty rough time, it seems.

233
00:16:02,740 --> 00:16:04,020
How is Sol holding up?

234
00:16:04,240 --> 00:16:05,660
Stein is operating on him now.

235
00:16:05,660 --> 00:16:08,160
He was hurt pretty bad, but I think he'll be all right.

236
00:16:09,100 --> 00:16:12,220
The demon sword has surfaced, and it's united with a Meister,

237
00:16:12,580 --> 00:16:14,820
actually embedded within him from what you say.

238
00:16:15,160 --> 00:16:17,220
And behind it all is a powerful witch.

239
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:26,260
Goodness, it looks like things are getting pretty crazy around here, aren't they?

240
00:16:26,500 --> 00:16:30,200
Oh, Lord Death, don't you think you might be taking this a little too lightly?

241
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:31,320
Oh?

242
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:39,720
How was your extra credit lesson?

243
00:16:40,380 --> 00:16:42,400
All in all, it went pretty well, I guess.

244
00:16:42,740 --> 00:16:45,720
Ugh, you're lucky. I have a remedial lesson tomorrow.

245
00:16:46,260 --> 00:16:48,340
Personally, I'd rather have a remedial lesson.

246
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:49,340
Didn't you hear?

247
00:16:50,160 --> 00:16:54,100
Apparently, a one-star kid named Soul Eater got injured and had to be brought back for surgery.

248
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:56,060
You're kidding. I hope he's all right.

249
00:16:57,160 --> 00:16:58,600
What? Something happened to Soul?

250
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:18,220
Professor Stein?

251
00:17:18,740 --> 00:17:21,480
Huh. Have you been waiting out here this whole time?

252
00:17:21,980 --> 00:17:24,140
Why didn't you go take a nap or eat or something?

253
00:17:24,600 --> 00:17:26,240
I need to know how Soul is!

254
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:31,020
The operation was a complete success.

255
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:34,160
Once he rests up a little bit, he'll be as good as new.

256
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:38,640
He's okay.

257
00:17:39,340 --> 00:17:40,920
Thank you so much, Professor.

258
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:43,120
Um.

259
00:17:43,860 --> 00:17:44,220
Hmm?

260
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:47,580
Would it be all right if I went in to check on him now?

261
00:17:48,580 --> 00:17:50,300
Sure. That'll be fine.

262
00:17:50,540 --> 00:17:51,120
Thank you.

263
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:51,180
Thank you.

264
00:17:51,180 --> 00:17:56,280
That's a nice, fake smile you're wearing.

265
00:18:01,880 --> 00:18:04,240
So tell me what you wouldn't tell Maka.

266
00:18:04,840 --> 00:18:06,280
What is Soul's condition, really?

267
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:16,260
The wound itself is all right after surgery. That much I can say, at least.

268
00:18:16,940 --> 00:18:19,340
But there is still something that bothers me.

269
